  "title": "ながら — while (doing both)",
  "pattern": "ます stem + ながら、B",
  "explanation": "ながら joins two actions one person does at the same time: {音楽|おんがく}を{聞|き}きながら{勉強|べんきょう}する — study while listening to music. Take the ます form, drop ます and add ながら: {食|た}べます → {食|た}べながら. The main action comes last.",
  "natural": "Everyday, any register: {歩|ある}きながら{話|はな}す, テレビを{見|み}ながら{食|た}べる.",
  "stiff": "Only for one person doing both things. For \"while you were out, I…\" — two people — Japanese uses {間|あいだ}に: {出|で}かけている{間|あいだ}に.",
